                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7e596bf-07b4-4923-a5ce-b7b849663660",
                                                "sense_id": "6d4979a7-8d82-3386-922e-eb2d67aef3fa",
                                                "text": "Reflection had given calmness to her judgment, and sobered her own opinion of Willoughby's deserts; — she wished, therefore, to declare only the simple truth, and lay open such facts as were really due to his character, without any embellishment of tenderness to lead the fancy astray."
